### Part 2: Step-by-Step Recording Guide

#### **1. Environment Setup (Before hitting record)**
*   **Zoom Level:** Set your Chrome or Edge zoom level to **150%**. This is crucial for making the code legible on mobile devices.
*   **Layout:** Split your screen to show [CodeEditor.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/CodeEditor.jsx) on the left (showing [test_date_helper.py](file:///d:/AntiMatter/backend/test_date_helper.py)) and the [Terminal.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/Terminal.jsx) on the right. Keep the [ChatPanel.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/ChatPanel.jsx) collapsed or empty.
*   **Recording Tool:** Use **OBS Studio** (Free, open-source) or **Loom** (set to 4K or 1080p, 60fps). Record only the active window (hide your browser tabs and bookmark bar).

#### **2. The Action Sequence (What to record)**
1.  **Start Recording:** Have the cursor focus on the [Terminal.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/Terminal.jsx) panel.
2.  **Trigger the Error:** Type `pytest test_date_helper.py` and press Enter. Let the red `ValueError` traceback fill the terminal.
3.  **The Log Redirect:** Hover your mouse over the terminal header and click the **"Send Logs to AI"** button (added in [README.md:L93](file:///d:/AntiMatter/README.md#L93)). 
4.  **Observe the Chat Input:** Watch the logs get pasted into the [ChatPanel.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/ChatPanel.jsx) input bar. Click the send button.
5.  **Let the Agent Work:** Keep the recording running as the agent calls tools in `tools.py` (e.g., reading `date_helper.py`, running tests).
6.  **The Diff:** When the git-style [DiffViewer.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/DiffViewer.jsx) pops up, scroll down it slowly to show the green replacement code (where the agent edits `strptime` to support both formats).
7.  **Apply and Verify:** Click **"Accept"** in the diff viewer. Switch back to the [Terminal.jsx](file:///d:/AntiMatter/frontend/src/components/Terminal.jsx) and run `pytest test_date_helper.py` again. Watch the tests pass with green text.
8.  **Stop Recording.**

