### Part 4: Visual Polish Tips for LinkedIn

*   **Dynamic Zoom (Ken Burns Effect):** When the focus transitions from the terminal to the chat, don't just cut—use a smooth camera pan/zoom in your editing software to make the transition look professional.
*   **CapCut Kinetic Subtitles:** Use CapCut's automated text effects. Style the subtitles in a high-contrast style (e.g., yellow and white text on a black outline/glow) using a modern font like **DM Sans** or **Inter**.
*   **Pacing (Speeding Up):** Real agent runs take time to stream tokens. Speed up the middle section of the video (where the agent is writing the code) by **3x to 5x** so the viewer doesn't lose interest. The entire video should feel snappy and move fast.

